─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MODDING PERMISSION
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Project Polychrome permits non-commercial modding under the following terms:

- Modders are allowed to extract game assets (including textures, models,
  animations, audio, and scripts) solely for the purpose of creating mods for
  Project Polychrome.

- Extracted assets may only be used within mods and may not be redistributed
  in their original, unmodified form.

- Mods must not include significant portions of original game content, and must
  not enable reconstruction, reproduction, or replacement of the full Software
  or its assets.

- Mods must be distributed only as user-created files, modified versions of
  extracted assets, or patch files that require the user to own an original
  copy of the Software.

- Mods must be strictly non-commercial. Selling, licensing, monetizing, or
  profiting from mods created using the Software or its assets is prohibited.

- Mods must not bypass or modify any copy protection, DRM, license checks, or
  systems intended to prevent unauthorized distribution or duplication.

- Mods must not include any tools, instructions, or methods for obtaining game
  assets without legally owning the Software.

- Mods must not facilitate piracy, redistribution, unauthorized asset sharing,
  or access to the Software by users who have not purchased it.

Violation of these terms revokes modding permission.

